  <p><strong>Effective 13 August 2026.</strong></p>
  <h2>What Chef stores</h2>
  <p>Household names, people, explicit dietary and safety constraints, preferences, meal plans, exact recipe versions, grocery plans, concise shop-run evidence and meal outcomes are stored in a SQLite database in the folder the user chooses.</p>
  <p>Only that folder's path is stored in a user-level Chef configuration file. Chef can create JSON, Markdown and SQLite backups when the user requests them.</p>

  <h2>What Chef does not store</h2>
  <p>Chef must not persist retailer credentials, cookies, payment information, screenshots or raw retailer pages. It does not send the local database to Daniel Ferguson.</p>
  <p>A host agent or optional Computer Use provider may process information under its own privacy terms. Review those terms before enabling browser automation.</p>

  <h2>Local protection and deletion</h2>
  <p>Chef permission-restricts its local files where the operating system supports it. Version 0.1 does not provide application-level encryption, so anyone with access to the operating-system account or backups may be able to read them.</p>
  <p>Users can export their data or remove the chosen data folder and Chef configuration themselves. Chef does not automate removal because that action is destructive.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:gday@danferg.com">gday@danferg.com</a>.</p>
</ChefPageLayout>
